{:edb/db-before-t 937 :edb/db-after-t 938 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534250 50 #inst "2026-10-11T18:15:39.199Z" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105459 1071 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=xz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x^2-y$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n![](images/69/69764cda6db58d51cf12ab33a352191513d3f572292203135108bfc15f902584.svg)\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105459 1071 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=xz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x^2-y$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n![](images/e4/e44b57bad88dcc1c13680f0e8f110696c6975b16c1d9553138fb6aeb4cadb8f9.png)\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534250 17592186045417 false] [17592186105887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415980 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415981 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415982 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105888 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415983 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105889 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415979 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186105951 1050 900.0 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186106060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102246 13194139534250 17592186045417 false] [17592186106060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415978 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186106060 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186106060 1071 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x, y, z) = 2xy$, where the surface $S$ is defined by $z = x^{2} + y^{2}$ for $-1 \\le x \\le 1$ and $0 \\le y \\le 2$.\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below.\n$∬_(S)f(x, y, z)dS = \\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}AAAAAAAdydx$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534250 17592186045417 false] [17592186106060 1071 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=2xy,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186106060 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(2x)}^{2}+{(2y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2xy\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,2xy\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186107153 1064 "Recall that for a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, if a surface is given by the explicit equation $z=g(x,y)$ over a plane region $D$ in Cartesian coordinates, then the canonical parametrization of this surface is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,y) = \\langle x,\\:  y, \\: g(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad (x,y) \\in D.\n$$\n\nMoreover, we know that under the canonical parametrization, the magnitude of the fundamental vector product is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{'}\\times {r}_{y}^{'}‖ & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f\\left(x,y,g(x,y)\\right) \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$" 13194139534250 17592186045417 false] [17592186107153 1064 "Recall that for a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, if a surface is given by the explicit equation $z=g(x,y)$ over a plane region $D$ in Cartesian coordinates, then the canonical parametrization of this surface is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,y) = \\langle x,\\:  y, \\: g(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad (x,y) \\in D.\n$$\n\nMoreover, we know that under the canonical parametrization, the magnitude of the fundamental vector product is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f\\left(x,y,g(x,y)\\right) \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415943 1080 "-21" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415943 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415943 1083 #uuid "008daf1a-a433-5118-aad3-61bc2cd82151" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415944 1080 "2xy\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415944 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415944 1083 #uuid "0be6bfb1-22ec-54d7-8d70-408044da5849" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415945 1080 "-18" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415945 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415945 1083 #uuid "11622f2c-a064-5989-bfd9-037259b1990a" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415946 1080 "2xy\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415946 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415946 1083 #uuid "11f496da-87e3-5a3b-81b0-ad4ccd99eec9" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415947 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415947 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415947 1083 #uuid "137ced3c-e27e-55d0-a129-d7f6d14ddfc4" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415948 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415948 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415948 1083 #uuid "193323db-4837-5978-b14e-f2ac7216eb5b" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415949 1080 "xy\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}" 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415949 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534250 17592186045417 true] [17592186415949 1083 #uuid "1ac43cfe-450e-5f00-a858-df79110cc719" 13194139534250 17592186045417 tru